 verdict set; a row either must be identical/spelled, or is listed as a documented gap with a reason string; the test FAILS if a row is better or worse than its expectation (so improvements force the expectation to be updated and regressions are caught). When CALIPER_BIN is missing the test skips with a clear message and the package test still passes; add a CI note in the README of the directory on how CI should build the binary (do not edit workflows). (4) A short README.md in apps/oracle/construct-suite/ explaining the layout, the two commands, how to add a row, and what green/gap means. Run the oracle package tests, tsc, `just lint doc-check machete typos` (read exit status) and a clean-room run per the rules; signed commits; plain push of feat/construct-suite; keep the seed rows. Report the exact commands, layout and anything the integrator must know.',
